+### Optional Persistence
+
+By default everything is ephemeral: a restart wipes uploaded files and the
+shared pad. To keep them across restarts, opt in per server — either in the
+server's config entry:
+
+```json
+"servers": { "main": { "url": "...", "persist-files": true, "persist-pad": true } }
+```
+
+or via environment variables (override config per-key):
+
+```bash
+COMPANION_PERSIST_FILES=1 COMPANION_PERSIST_PAD=1 python companion.py server
+```
+
+With `persist-files` on, uploaded blobs are stored under the state dir
+(`servers/<name>/files/blobs/<uuid>` plus a `files/index.json` metadata
+index) and file content is no longer held in memory — it is read from disk
+on download. The pad is mirrored to `servers/<name>/pad.json` on every
+update. Both are reloaded at startup; blobs with no index entry (e.g. from
+an interrupted write) are swept away. The preview state stays ephemeral —
+it is a live-session concept.
+
